            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "S&P 500 Movers: Equifax Hits Back At FICO In Credit Score Wars",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Equifax has slashed prices for mortgage credit scores in response to Fair Isaac's move last week that aimed to limit the mortgage industry's reliance on credit bureaus.  FICO was the biggest laggard on the S&P 500, giving back a big chunk of last week's gains, while Equifax recovered some of last week's losses.  The backdrop is that FICO has been under pressure from Bill Pulte, director of the Federal Housing Finance Agency, who said in July that government-backed mortgage giants Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac will now allow lenders to use VantageScore 4.0 as an alternative to the traditional FICO score.",
